ccurrence. This line's end-rhyme is UNKNOWN, not absent.","locations":[15,16],"groups":["E"],"obligations":[],"subject":["unreadable_anchor",16]},{"code":"SUBSTITUTED_END_WORD","severity":"note","message":"1 line(s) would have had the RHYME WORD SILENTLY REPLACED by an earlier word: L16 '1999'->'since'","evidence":"`word_syllable_map` emits no syllable for a word CMUdict cannot read, so anything taking its last entry as the rhyme word takes an EARLIER word instead -- the defect the shipped file carried in `_qafiya_parts`, where `zun` reported as `the` and `grow'st` as `thou`. THIS IS NOT A SECOND CHARGE. 1 of these 1 line(s) are ALREADY flagged above by UNREADABLE_END_WORD, which says the LINE cannot be read; what no other finding in this module says is WHICH WORD would have been used, and that is the only part a writer or a caller can act on -- the substitute is a plausible English word, so nothing about the output looks wrong. Every one of them is also flagged above, so this finding adds the word and no new line.","locations":[16],"groups":[],"obligations":[[16]],"subject":[]},{"code":"SPARSE","severity":"note","message":"fewer syllables than pulses — pulses with nothing declared on them","evidence":"9 syllables over 7 pulses leaves 110 pulses unaccounted for. Where they fall is a setting question and is refused below. READ AS: us = 1 syllable .","locations":[16],"groups":[],"obligations":[],"subject":[]},{"code":"HEADS_EXCEED_UNITS","severity":"note","message":"more group heads than syllables — at least 42 head carries nothing at all","evidence":"9 syllables against 51 heads at pulses ('b256.1', 'b256.3', 'b256.5', 'b257.1', 'b257.3', 'b257.5', 'b258.1', 'b258.3', 'b258.5', 'b259.1', 'b259.3', 'b259.5', 'b260.1', 'b260.3', 'b260.5', 'b261.1', 'b261.3', 'b261.5', 'b262.1', 'b262.3', 'b262.5', 'b263.1', 'b263.3', 'b263.5', 'b264.1', 'b264.3', 'b264.5', 'b265.1', 'b265.3', 'b265.5', 'b266.1', 'b266.3', 'b266.5', 'b267.1', 'b267.3', 'b267.5', 'b268.1', 'b268.3', 'b26